{"id":"supergraphic-ultramodern","title":"Supergraphic Ultramodern","url":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/Supergraphic_Ultramodern","rev":236548,"fetched":"2026-10-16","lead":[{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"b","c":["Supergraphic Ultramodern"]}," is a futuristic design aesthetic that was popular from the 1970s to early 1980s, succeeding ",{"t":"a","c":["Raygun Gothic"],"id":"raygun-gothic"},", ",{"t":"a","c":["Space Age"],"id":"space-age"},", ",{"t":"a","c":["Googie"],"href":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/Googie"},", ",{"t":"a","c":["Atompunk"],"href":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/Atompunk"},", and ",{"t":"a","c":["Mid-Century Modern"],"id":"mid-century-modern"}," and overlapping with ",{"t":"a","c":["Earth Tones"],"id":"earth-tones"}," and ",{"t":"a","c":["Cassette Futurism"],"href":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/Cassette_Futurism"},"."]}],"sections":[{"title":"History","id":"history","blocks":[{"t":"p","c":["Supergraphic Ultramodern was first seen in late 1960s New Hollywood films, such as ",{"t":"i","c":["2001: A Space Odyssey"]},". By the 1970s it grew to become a dominant aesthetic in sci-fi, seen in movies such as ",{"t":"i","c":["Logan's Run"]},". In the mid-1980s, Ultramodern was supplanted by newer aesthetics such as ",{"t":"a","c":["Cyberpunk"],"href":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/Cyberpunk"},"/",{"t":"a","c":["Laser Grid"],"id":"laser-grid"},", ",{"t":"a","c":["Cassette Futurism"],"href":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/Cassette_Futurism"},", and ",{"t":"a","c":["Memphis Lite"],"id":"memphis-lite"},"."]}]},{"title":"Visuals","id":"visuals","blocks":[{"t":"p","c":["Supergraphic Ultramodern focuses on interiors that are often white, orange, or rainbow-colored, flat graphics, iconography, inflatable furniture, and materials like plastics, plush, fiberglass, and shiny metals. Ultramodern contains curvy/rounded designs, similar to its predecessor Mid-Century Modern, but often with more earth-toned colors such as brown or orange."]}]},{"title":"Ultramodern Revival","id":"ultramodern-revival","blocks":[{"t":"p","c":["With nostalgia for the 1970s taking over pop culture in the mid-late 1990s, Supergraphic Ultramodern would be included in this general revival. This style's return was retroactively named ",{"t":"a","c":["Ultramodern Revival"],"href":"https://cari.institute/aesthetics/ultramodern-revival"},", and was relevant ca. late 1990s to the mid 2000s. It had similarity to ",{"t":"a","c":["Millennium Disco"],"href":"https://cari.institute/aesthetics/millennium-disco"}," and ",{"t":"a","c":["Gen X Soft Club"],"href":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/Gen_X_Soft_Club"}," through their shared nostalgia for the 1970s."]},{"t":"p","c":["Supergraphic Ultramodern, ",{"t":"a","c":["Mid-Century Modern"],"id":"mid-century-modern"},", and ",{"t":"a","c":["Space Age"],"id":"space-age"}," would serve as major influences to the ",{"t":"a","c":["Y2K Futurism"],"id":"y2k-futurism"}," aesthetic."]},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/c/c3/D%27Edge_Nightclub_%281999%29.png/revision/latest?cb=20260306200739","w":185,"h":185,"cap":["D'Edge Nightclub (1999)"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/2/26/Mystery_Inc._HQ_-_Scooby_Doo_2-_Monsters_Unleashed_%282004%29.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20260306200824","w":185,"h":185,"cap":["Mystery Inc. HQ - Scooby Doo 2- Monsters Unleashed (2004)"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/f/f0/Austin_Power%27s_home-apartment_in_Goldemember_%282002%29.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20260306200912","w":185,"h":185,"cap":["Austin Power's home-apartment in Goldemember (2002)"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/c/ce/Groove_Sanctuary_%E2%80%93_Various_%282002%29.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20260306200933","w":185,"h":185,"cap":["Groove Sanctuary – Various (2002)"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/8/8e/Pizzicato_Five_%E2%80%93_The_Fifth_Release_From_Matador_%282000%29.png/revision/latest?cb=20260306200947","w":185,"h":185,"cap":["Pizzicato Five ‎– The Fifth Release From Matador (2000)"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/0/09/AIR_%E2%80%93_Premiers_Symptomes_%281997-1999%29.png/revision/latest?cb=20260306201033","w":185,"h":185,"cap":["AIR ‎– Premiers Symptomes (1997/1999)"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/8/80/The_Strawberry_Smell_-_Odorama_%282002%29.png/revision/latest?cb=20260306201055","w":185,"h":185,"cap":["The Strawberry Smell - Odorama (2002)"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/e/e0/Pizzicato_Five_%E2%80%93_Expo_2001_%281993%29.png/revision/latest?cb=20260306201108","w":185,"h":185,"cap":["Pizzicato Five – Expo 2001 (1993)"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/e/eb/Luke_Slater_%E2%80%93_Alright_On_Top_%282002%29.png/revision/latest?cb=20260306201154","w":185,"h":185,"cap":["Luke Slater ‎– Alright On Top (2002)"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/6/69/The_Bay_Commercial_2001_%22Get_on_up%22/revision/latest?cb=20260307161515","w":185,"h":185}]},{"t":"p","c":["Ultramodern, Earth Tones, and Laser Grid would go on to serve as inspiration for ",{"t":"a","c":["Cassette Retrofuturism"],"href":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/Cassette_Futurism"}," in the 2000s to 2020s. In 2023, musician Chapelle Roan released the song \"Super Graphic Ultra Modern Girl\", which featured 1970s–80s ",{"t":"a","c":["Glam Rock"],"href":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/Glam_Rock"}," influences in its music video."]}]},{"title":"Media","id":"media","blocks":[{"t":"h","l":3,"c":["Film"]},{"t":"ul","items":[{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["2001: A Space Odyssey"]}," (1968)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Planet of the Apes"]}," (1968)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["The Andromeda Strain"]}," (1971)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Willy Wonka & the Chocolate Factory"]}," (1971)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Silent Running"]}," (1972)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Solaris"]}," (1972)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Westworld"]}," (1973)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Logan's Run"]}," (1976)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Star Wars: A New Hope"]}," (1977), ",{"t":"i","c":["The Empire Strikes Back"]}," (1980) and ",{"t":"i","c":["Return of the Jedi"]}," (1983)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Alien"]}," (1979)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Outland"]}," (1981)"]}]},{"t":"h","l":3,"c":["Games"]},{"t":"ul","items":[{"c":["American Arcadia (2023)"]},{"c":["Headlander (2016)"]}]}]},{"title":"Resources","id":"resources","blocks":[{"t":"ul","items":[{"c":[{"t":"a","c":["https://cari.institute/aesthetics/supergraphic-ultramodern"],"href":"https://cari.institute/aesthetics/supergraphic-ultramodern"}]},{"c":[{"t":"a","c":["https://cari.institute/aesthetics/ultramodern-revival"],"href":"https://cari.institute/aesthetics/ultramodern-revival"}]},{"c":[{"t":"a","c":["https://www.are.na/evan-collins-1522646491/supergraphic-ultramodern"],"href":"https://www.are.na/evan-collins-1522646491/supergraphic-ultramodern"}]},{"c":[{"t":"a","c":["https://www.are.na/evan-collins-1522646491/ultramodern-revival"],"href":"https://www.are.na/evan-collins-1522646491/ultramodern-revival"}]}]}]},{"title":"Gallery","id":"gallery","blocks":[{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"i","c":["[Under Construction]"]}]},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/3/34/Visiona_II_%281970%29_1.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20260226202807","w":185,"h":185,"cap":["Visiona II (1970), Verner Panton"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/4/41/Visiona_II_%281970%29_2.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20260226202832","w":185,"h":185,"cap":["Visiona II (1970), Verner Panton"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/5/50/Visiona_II_%281970%29_3.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20260226202847","w":185,"h":185,"cap":["Visiona II (1970), Verner Panton"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/3/39/Atari_Headquarters_Interior_%281976%29_1.png/revision/latest?cb